   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1: Number of submissions made by NHRC- B to international human rights instruments /mechanisms (Human rights council, UPR, treaty bodies and special procedures.
1.2: Number of dialogues/ consultations held by NHRC with government authorities and CSOs for preparation of reports to international Human Rights mechanisms.
2.1: Number of coalitions formed through the challenge fund to advance Human Rights initiatives/actions of CSOs/CBOs at grassroots level.
2.2: Number of rights forums jointly undertaken by NHRC thematic committees and CSOs to discuss contemporary human right issues.
3.1: Number of cases reported against law enforcement agencies and police to NHRC.
3.2: Number of times the police take part in human rights dialogues with the NHRC and CSOs.
4.1: % of school students (including teachers) that have a better understanding on women and girl&#x2019;s rights after campaigns.
4.2: Number of complaints of women&#x2019;s rights violations submitted to the NHRC by the Committee on Violence Against Women and Children (NNPC) and CSOs/CBOs.
5.1: Number of community radio stations broadcasting minority language programming and rights education programmes.
5.2: % of youth leaders trained have become active in transforming their leadership role to promote the rights of ethnic minorities.
6.1: Number of judges and public prosecutors have adequate knowledge to deal with a digitalized case management system
6.2: Number of High Court benches record system digitalized on commercial nature.</narrative>
    </description>
